# Encrypted by transcrypt. The `text=auto eol=lf` normalizes the base64 ciphertext on the way into the blob,
# which is what stops a Windows clone and a macOS clone re-encrypting each other's commits forever. Never
# replace it with `-text`, and do not drop it to match upstream's bare line — upstream has no Windows story.
#
# The pattern is the `*.secret.*` naming convention rather than a path, so a secret file added
# anywhere in the repo is covered the moment it is named — and a file that forgets the marker is
# stopped by the global pre-commit hook rather than leaking past a rule nobody remembered to extend.
*.secret.* filter=crypt diff=crypt merge=crypt text=auto eol=lf
